  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let G be a nilpotent group in which every coset x[G, G] for x ̸∈ [G, G]\ncoincides with the conjugacy class xG . Is there a bound for the nilpotency class of G?\n    If G is finite, then its class is at most 3 (R. Dark, C. Scoppola, J. Algebra, 181,\nno. 3 (1996), 787–802).                                    S. H. Ghate, A. S. Muktibodh",
